# Commits that only reformat, which `git blame` should look through to the change before them.
#
# GitHub's blame view reads this file automatically. Locally, run once:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Each entry is a formatting-only commit as it landed on dev. Only a merge commit keeps these SHAs: a
# squash rewrites them, and an entry then names a commit that is not in the history, which blame ignores
# silently. The repository's ruleset offers only squash, so a pull request carrying an entry must be
# merged with `gh pr merge --merge` through the bypass, and
# `git merge-base --is-ancestor <sha> origin/dev` confirms it landed. A formatter version bump adds its
# own entry (ADR-037, ADR-038).

